{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"B7JB88","uniProtkbId":"ATPF_ACIF2","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2009-04-14","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2009-02-10","entryVersion":80,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":2.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Acidithiobacillus ferrooxidans (strain ATCC 23270 / DSM 14882 / CIP 104768 / NCIMB 8455)","commonName":"Ferrobacillus ferrooxidans (strain ATCC 23270)","taxonId":243159,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Acidithiobacillia","Acidithiobacillales","Acidithiobacillaceae","Acidithiobacillus"]},"proteinExistence":"3: Inferred from homology","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"ATP synthase subunit b"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"ATP synthase F(0) sector subunit b"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"ATPase subunit I"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"F-type ATPase subunit b"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"F-ATPase subunit b"}]}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"atpF"},"orderedLocusNames":[{"value":"AFE_3207"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"F(1)F(0) ATP synthase produces ATP from ADP in the presence of a proton or sodium gradient. F-type ATPases consist of two structural domains, F(1) containing the extramembraneous catalytic core and F(0) containing the membrane proton channel, linked together by a central stalk and a peripheral stalk. During catalysis, ATP synthesis in the catalytic domain of F(1) is coupled via a rotary mechanism of the central stalk subunits to proton translocation"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"Component of the F(0) channel, it forms part of the peripheral stalk, linking F(1) to F(0)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"F-type ATPases have 2 components, F(1) - the catalytic core - and F(0) - the membrane proton channel. F(1) has five subunits: alpha(3), beta(3), gamma(1), delta(1), epsilon(1). F(0) has three main subunits: a(1), b(2) and c(10-14). The alpha and beta chains form an alternating ring which encloses part of the gamma chain. F(1) is attached to F(0) by a central stalk formed by the gamma and epsilon chains, while a peripheral stalk is formed by the delta and b chains"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"Cell inner membrane","id":"SL-0037"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"Single-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9904"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}],"value":"Belongs to the ATPase B chain family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":159,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"ATP synthase subunit b","featureId":"PRO_0000368283"},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":4,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":24,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01398"}]}],"keywords":[{"id":"KW-0066","category":"Biological process","name":"ATP synth